{"id":"h06t3","name":"Hourly Latency Report","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>requests</b> has the columns <code>req_id</code>, <code>service</code>, <code>ts</code> (timestamp), <code>latency_ms</code> and <code>status</code> (HTTP status code). A request is an <b>error</b> when its status is 500 or more.</p>\n<p>Build an hourly report for each service. It must contain <b>every hour</b> from the hour of the first request of the service to the hour of its last request, including hours with no request at all. An hour is written as the timestamp truncated to the hour.</p>\n<p>For each service and hour, compute <code>requests</code> (number of requests), <code>errors</code>, <code>p95_ms</code> (the 95th percentile of the latency of the <b>non-error</b> requests, continuous interpolation, rounded to 1 decimal, <code>NULL</code> when there is no such request) and <code>change_pct</code>: the percentage change of <code>p95_ms</code> compared to the previous hour of the same service, computed from the rounded values as <code>100 * (current - previous) / previous</code> and rounded to 1 decimal. <code>change_pct</code> is <code>NULL</code> when one of the two values is <code>NULL</code> or when the previous value is 0.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>service</code>, <code>hour</code>, <code>requests</code>, <code>errors</code>, <code>p95_ms</code> and <code>change_pct</code>, sorted by <code>service</code>, then <code>hour</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>requests</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>req_id</th><th>service</th><th>ts</th><th>latency_ms</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>100</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>200</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 08:20:00</td><td>900</td><td>503</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>300</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 11:05:00</td><td>120</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 11:10:00</td><td>80</td><td>404</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>auth</td><td>2026-03-02 08:05:00</td><td>50</td><td>500</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>auth</td><td>2026-03-02 09:10:00</td><td>40</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>auth</td><td>2026-03-02 09:15:00</td><td>60</td><td>200</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>service</th><th>hour</th><th>requests</th><th>errors</th><th>p95_ms</th><th>change_pct</th></tr><tr><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>290.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>api</td><td>2026-03-02 11:00:00</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>118.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>auth</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>auth</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>59.0</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>requests</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>service</code>, <code>hour</code>, <code>requests</code>, <code>errors</code>, <code>p95_ms</code>, <code>change_pct</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["generate_series","heures vides","percentile_cont","FILTER","LAG"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>requests</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>service</code>, <code>hour</code>, <code>requests</code>, <code>errors</code>, <code>p95_ms</code>, <code>change_pct</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM:SS pour une date avec heure.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"requests":{"columns":[["req_id","INT"],["service","TEXT"],["ts","TIMESTAMP"],["latency_ms","INT"],["status","INT"]],"rows":[[1,"api","2026-03-02 08:00:00",100,200],[2,"api","2026-03-02 08:10:00",200,200],[3,"api","2026-03-02 08:20:00",900,503],[4,"api","2026-03-02 08:30:00",300,200],[5,"api","2026-03-02 11:05:00",120,200],[6,"api","2026-03-02 11:10:00",80,404],[7,"auth","2026-03-02 08:05:00",50,500],[8,"auth","2026-03-02 09:10:00",40,200],[9,"auth","2026-03-02 09:15:00",60,200]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["service","hour","requests","errors","p95_ms","change_pct"],"rows":[["api","2026-03-02 08:00:00",4,1,290.0,null],["api","2026-03-02 09:00:00",0,0,null,null],["api","2026-03-02 10:00:00",0,0,null,null],["api","2026-03-02 11:00:00",2,0,118.0,null],["auth","2026-03-02 08:00:00",1,1,null,null],["auth","2026-03-02 09:00:00",2,0,59.0,null]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"requests":{"columns":[["req_id","INT"],["service","TEXT"],["ts","TIMESTAMP"],["latency_ms","INT"],["status","INT"]],"rows":[[1,"pay","2026-03-02 08:00:00",0,200],[2,"pay","2026-03-02 09:05:00",30,200],[3,"pay","2026-03-02 10:10:00",10,502],[4,"pay","2026-03-02 11:20:00",20,200]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["service","hour","requests","errors","p95_ms","change_pct"],"rows":[["pay","2026-03-02 08:00:00",1,0,0.0,null],["pay","2026-03-02 09:00:00",1,0,30.0,null],["pay","2026-03-02 10:00:00",1,1,null,null],["pay","2026-03-02 11:00:00",1,0,20.0,null]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}